From 5412bbcf27db50adf35ea2072a22977fd8ba675d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:56:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: cpufreq: apple,cluster-cpufreq: Add T6050

The T6050 (M5 Pro/Max) cluster DVFS block has the T8112 register layout:
on the J716s the status register at +0x50 carries the current p-state in
bits 9:5 and the target in bits 4:0, as on T8112, and stock
apple-soc-cpufreq drives all three clusters through the
"apple,t8112-cluster-cpufreq" fallback with max_pstate 31.

Allow "apple,t6050-cluster-cpufreq" with that fallback, as for T6020,
T6030, T6031, T6041 and T8122. A later driver entry for T6050 itself
(the j716c/t6050-platform branch has one, with transition verification
and a firmware-thermal requirement) matches the first string and takes
precedence without a device tree change.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml       | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml
index 84e5ce2657dc..f43bfc4fb9f3 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml
@@ -45,6 +45,7 @@ properties:
               - apple,t6030-cluster-cpufreq
               - apple,t6031-cluster-cpufreq
               - apple,t6041-cluster-cpufreq
+              - apple,t6050-cluster-cpufreq
               - apple,t8122-cluster-cpufreq
           - const: apple,t8112-cluster-cpufreq
 
